{:edb/db-before-t 1916 :edb/db-after-t 1917 :edb/tx-data [[13194139535229 50 #inst "2026-10-08T20:03:05.106Z" 13194139535229 true] [17592186119577 1100 "Find the intersection point of the line $l$ and the plane $\\Pi$ with equations\n\n$$\nl: \\mathbf{r} = \\langle 5,3,-4 \\rangle + t \\langle 4,-2,-3 \\rangle, \\qquad \t\\Pi: \\mathbf{r} \\cdot \\langle -7,5,1 \\rangle = -65.\n$$" 13194139535229 true] [17592186119577 1100 "Find the intersection point of the line $l$ and the plane $\\Pi$ with equations\n$l: \\mathbf{r} = \\langle 5,3,-4 \\rangle + t \\langle 4,-2,-3 \\rangle, \\qquad \\Pi: \\mathbf{r} \\cdot \\langle -7,5,1 \\rangle = -65$." 13194139535229 false] [17592186119577 1145 "Let's write the equation of the line as\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{r} = \\langle 5+4t, 3-2t, -4-3t \\rangle\n$$\n\nNow, substituting\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{r} = \\langle 5+4t, 3-2t, -4-3t \\rangle\n$$\n\ninto the equation of the plane, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nr \\cdot ⟨ - 7, 5, 1⟩ &= -65 \\\\\n⟨5 + 4t, 3 - 2t,-4 - 3t⟩ \\cdot ⟨ - 7, 5, 1⟩ &= -65 \\\\\n- 7(5 + 4t) + 5(3 - 2t) + (-4 - 3t) &= -65 \\\\\n- 35 - 28t + 15 - 10t - 4 - 3t &= -65 \\\\\n- 41t &= -41 \\\\\nt &= 1\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the position vector $\\mathbf{p}$ of the intersection point is obtained by substituting $t=1$ into the equation of the line, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\np &= ⟨5 + 4(1), 3 - 2(1),-4 - 3(1)⟩ \\\\\n&= ⟨9, 1,-7⟩\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the intersection point is $P(9, 1, -7)$." 13194139535229 false] [17592186119577 1145 "Let's write the equation of the line as \n\n$$\n\\mathbf{r} = \\langle 5+4t , 3-2t, -4-3t \\rangle.\n$$\n\nNow, substituting $\\mathbf{r} = \\langle 5+4t , 3-2t, -4-3t \\rangle$ into the equation of the plane, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r\\cdot ⟨-7,5,1⟩ & =-65 \\\\ ⟨5+4t,3-2t,-4-3t⟩\\cdot ⟨-7,5,1⟩ & =-65 \\\\ -7(5+4t)+5(3-2t)+(-4-3t) & =-65 \\\\ -35-28t+15-10t-4-3t & =-65 \\\\ -41t & =-41 \\\\ t & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the position vector $\\mathbf{p}$ of the intersection point is obtained by substituting $t=1$ into the equation of the line, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p & =⟨5+4(1),3-2(1),-4-3(1)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨9,1,-7⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the intersection point is $P(9 , 1, -7).$" 13194139535229 true] [17592186119578 1100 "Find the intersection point of the line $l$ and the plane $\\Pi$ with equations\n\n$$\nl: \\mathbf{r} = \\langle 1,3,1 \\rangle + t \\langle 2,1,0 \\rangle, \\qquad  \\Pi:4x-3y+2z-7 = 0.\n$$" 13194139535229 true] [17592186119578 1100 "Find the intersection point of the line $l$ and the plane $\\Pi$ with equations\n$l: \\mathbf{r} = \\langle 1,3,1 \\rangle + t \\langle 2,1,0 \\rangle, \\qquad \\Pi:4x-3y+2z-7 = 0$." 13194139535229 false] [17592186119578 1145 "Let's start by writing the equation of the line as\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{r} = \\langle 1+2t , 3+t, 1 \\rangle .\n$$\n\nLet's also write the equation of the plane in the dot product form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4x-3y+2z-7 & =0 \\\\ 4x-3y+2z & =7 \\\\ ⟨x,y,z⟩\\cdot ⟨4,-3,2⟩ & =7 \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨4,-3,2⟩ & =7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, substituting $\\mathbf{r} = \\langle 1+2t , 3+t, 1 \\rangle$ into the equation of the plane, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r\\cdot ⟨4,-3,2⟩ & =7 \\\\ ⟨1+2t,3+t,1⟩\\cdot ⟨4,-3,2⟩ & =7 \\\\ 4(1+2t)-3(3+t)+2\\cdot 1 & =7 \\\\ 4+8t-9-3t+2 & =7 \\\\ 5t & =10 \\\\ t & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, to get the position vector $\\mathbf{p}$ of the intersection point $P,$ we substitute $t=2$ into the equation of the line:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p & =⟨1+2(2),3+(2),1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨5,5,1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the intersection point is $P(5 , 5, 1).$" 13194139535229 true] [17592186119578 1145 "Let's start by writing the equation of the line as\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{r} = \\langle 1+2t, 3+t, 1 \\rangle\n$$\n\nLet's also write the equation of the plane in the dot product form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n4x - 3y + 2z - 7 &= 0 \\\\\n4x - 3y + 2z &= 7 \\\\\n⟨x, y, z⟩ \\cdot ⟨4,-3, 2⟩ &= 7 \\\\\nr \\cdot ⟨4,-3, 2⟩ &= 7\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, substituting\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{r} = \\langle 1+2t, 3+t, 1 \\rangle\n$$\n\ninto the equation of the plane, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nr \\cdot ⟨4,-3, 2⟩ &= 7 \\\\\n⟨1 + 2t, 3 + t, 1⟩ \\cdot ⟨4,-3, 2⟩ &= 7 \\\\\n4(1 + 2t) - 3(3 + t) + 2 \\cdot 1 &= 7 \\\\\n4 + 8t - 9 - 3t + 2 &= 7 \\\\\n5t &= 10 \\\\\nt &= 2\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, to get the position vector $\\mathbf{p}$ of the intersection point $P$, we substitute $t=2$ into the equation of the line:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\np &= ⟨1 + 2(2), 3 + (2), 1⟩ \\\\\n&= ⟨5, 5, 1⟩\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the intersection point is $P(5, 5, 1)$." 13194139535229 false] [17592186119579 1100 "Find the intersection point of the line $l$ and the plane $\\Pi$ with equations\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059450/assets/2a24a49f0fc47c235776597df655e75be9c68cffbb7988db16b36d9200f801bc.png)" 13194139535229 true] [17592186119579 1100 "Find the intersection point of the line $l$ and the plane $\\Pi$ with equations\n${x = 3 - 4t; y =-1 + 2t; z = 2 + 3t$" 13194139535229 false] [17592186119579 1145 "We can substitute the parametric expressions for $x$, $y$, and $z$ of the line into the equation of the plane immediately:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n3x + 4y + 6z + 25 &= 0 \\\\\n3(3 - 4t) + 4(-1 + 2t) + 6(2 + 3t) + 25 &= 0 \\\\\n9 - 12t - 4 + 8t + 12 + 18t + 25 &= 0 \\\\\n14t &= -42 \\\\\nt &= -3\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo get the position vector $\\mathbf{p}$ of the intersection point $P$, we substitute $t=-3$ into the parametric equations of the line:\n\n$$\n{x = 3 - 4(-3) = 15; y =-1 + 2(-3) =-7; z = 2 + 3(-3) =-7\n$$\n\nSo, the intersection point is $P(15,-7,-7)$." 13194139535229 false] [17592186119579 1145 "We can substitute the parametric expressions for $x,$ $y,$ and $z$ of the line into the equation of the plane immediately:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3x+4y+6z+25 & =0 \\\\ 3(3-4t)+4(-1+2t)+6(2+3t)+25 & =0 \\\\ 9-12t-4+8t+12+18t+25 & =0 \\\\ 14t & =-42 \\\\ t & =-3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo get the position vector $\\mathbf{p}$ of the intersection point $P$, we substitute $t=-3$ into the parametric equations of the line:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=3-4(-3)=15 \\\\ y=-1+2(-3)=-7 \\\\ z=2+3(-3)=-7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the intersection point is $P(15,-7,-7).$" 13194139535229 true] [17592186119760 1020 #edb/ref 17592186338723 13194139535229 true] [17592186119760 1020 #edb/ref 17592186338730 13194139535229 true] [17592186119760 1020 #edb/ref 17592186338786 13194139535229 true] [17592186119760 1020 #edb/ref 17592186338793 13194139535229 true] [17592186119760 1020 #edb/ref 17592186338800 13194139535229 true] [17592186119761 1020 #edb/ref 17592186338758 13194139535229 true] [17592186119761 1020 #edb/ref 17592186338765 13194139535229 true] [17592186119761 1020 #edb/ref 17592186338772 13194139535229 true] [17592186119761 1020 #edb/ref 17592186338779 13194139535229 true] [17592186119762 1020 #edb/ref 17592186338737 13194139535229 true] [17592186119762 1020 #edb/ref 17592186338744 13194139535229 true] [17592186119762 1020 #edb/ref 17592186338751 13194139535229 true] [17592186119762 1020 #edb/ref 17592186338807 13194139535229 true] [17592186119762 1020 #edb/ref 17592186338814 13194139535229 true] [17592186120172 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535229 true] [17592186120172 1100 "Find the intersection point of the line $l$ and the plane $Π$ with equations\n\n$$\nl:r=⟨-5,0,1⟩+t⟨-3,1,0⟩,\\,Π:-3x+y-2z+27=0.\n$$" 13194139535229 true] [17592186120172 1100 "Find the intersection point of the line $l$ and the plane $Π$ with equations\n\n$l: r = ⟨ - 5, 0, 1⟩ + t⟨ - 3, 1, 0⟩, Π: - 3x + y - 2z + 27 = 0$." 13194139535229 false] [17592186120172 1145 "Let's start by writing the equation of the line as\n\n$$\nr=⟨-5-3t,t,1⟩.\n$$\n\nLet's also write the equation of the plane in the dot product form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-3x+y-2z+27 & =0 \\\\ -3x+y-2z & =-27 \\\\ ⟨x,y,z⟩\\cdot ⟨-3,1,-2⟩ & =-27 \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨-3,1,-2⟩ & =-27\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, substituting $r=⟨-5-3t,t,1⟩$ into the equation of the plane, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r\\cdot ⟨-3,1,-2⟩ & =-27 \\\\ ⟨-5-3t,t,1⟩\\cdot ⟨-3,1,-2⟩ & =-27 \\\\ -3(-5-3t)+1\\cdot t-2\\cdot 1 & =-27 \\\\ 15+9t+t-2 & =-27 \\\\ 10t & =-40 \\\\ t & =-4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, to get the position vector $p$ of the intersection point $P,$ we substitute $t=-4$ into the equation of the line:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p & =⟨-5-3(-4),-4,1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨7,-4,1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the intersection point is $P(7,-4,1).$" 13194139535229 true] [17592186338723 1017 #edb/ref 17592186338724 13194139535229 true] [17592186338723 1089 "q-108311" 13194139535229 true] [17592186338723 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535229 true] [17592186338723 1100 "Find the intersection point of the line $l$ and the plane $Π$ with equations\n\n$$\nl:r=⟨5,-2,3⟩+t⟨0,3,-1⟩,\\,Π:r\\cdot ⟨1,3,-2⟩=-7.\n$$" 13194139535229 true] [17592186338723 1113 #uuid "8d28c265-18d6-5656-afcf-7f8222829274" 13194139535229 true] [17592186338723 1145 "Let's write the equation of the line as\n\n$$\nr=⟨5,-2+3t,3-t⟩.\n$$\n\nNow, substituting $r=⟨5,-2+3t,3-t⟩$ into the equation of the plane, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r\\cdot ⟨1,3,-2⟩ & =-7 \\\\ ⟨5,-2+3t,3-t⟩\\cdot ⟨1,3,-2⟩ & =-7 \\\\ 5+3(-2+3t)+(-2)(3-t) & =-7 \\\\ 5-6+9t-6+2t & =-7 \\\\ 11t & =0 \\\\ t & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, position vector $p$ of the intersection point $P$ is obtained by substituting $t=0$ into the equation of the line, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p & =⟨5,-2+3(0),3-0⟩ \\\\  & =⟨5,-2,3⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the intersection point is $P(5,-2,3).$" 13194139535229 true] [17592186338724 1000 #edb/ref 17592186338725 13194139535229 true] [17592186338724 1000 #edb/ref 17592186338726 13194139535229 true] [17592186338724 1000 #edb/ref 17592186338727 13194139535229 true] [17592186338724 1000 #edb/ref 17592186338728 13194139535229 true] [17592186338724 1000 #edb/ref 17592186338729 13194139535229 tru