229 true] [17592186338751 1145 "We can substitute the parametric expressions for $x,$ $y,$ and $z$ of the line into the equation of the plane immediately:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4x+3y+5z-11 & =0 \\\\ 4(9-3t)+3(5+2t)+5(-7+t) & =11 \\\\ 36-12t+15+6t-35+5t & =11 \\\\ -t & =-5 \\\\ t & =5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo get the position vector $p$ of the intersection point $P$, we substitute $t=5$ into the parametric equations of the line:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=9-3(5)=-6 \\\\ y=5+2(5)=15 \\\\ z=-7+5=-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the intersection point is  $P(-6,15,-2).$" 13194139535229 true] [17592186338752 1000 #edb/ref 17592186338753 13194139535229 true] [17592186338752 1000 #edb/ref 17592186338754 13194139535229 true] [17592186338752 1000 #edb/ref 17592186338755 13194139535229 true] [17592186338752 1000 #edb/ref 17592186338756 13194139535229 true] [17592186338752 1000 #edb/ref 17592186338757 13194139535229 true] [17592186338752 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535229 true] [17592186338752 1041 "selection" 13194139535229 true] [17592186338752 1104 #edb/ref 17592186338753 13194139535229 true] [17592186338752 1110 #uuid "6aabbaa0-da27-5e13-92cc-3d64261bc76d" 13194139535229 true] [17592186338753 1034 "(-6,15,-2)" 13194139535229 true] [17592186338753 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535229 true] [17592186338753 1111 #uuid "0685c34e-7f8c-542c-a8df-082d2bd2d0dd" 13194139535229 true] [17592186338754 1034 "(-3,13,-3)" 13194139535229 true] [17592186338754 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535229 true] [17592186338754 1111 #uuid "0ebcf735-1d00-575e-9786-8bd7db6f13d7" 13194139535229 true] [17592186338755 1034 "No intersection" 13194139535229 true] [17592186338755 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535229 true] [17592186338755 1111 #uuid "9c7549da-aa05-5f9a-b970-554a5ae24af8" 13194139535229 true] [17592186338756 1034 "(3,9,-5)" 13194139535229 true] [17592186338756 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535229 true] [17592186338756 1111 #uuid "55bad4ad-1cc1-5384-974a-a376f90f80bb" 13194139535229 true] [17592186338757 1034 "(18,-1,-10)" 13194139535229 true] [17592186338757 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535229 true] [17592186338757 1111 #uuid "4847ee0f-9e5c-5369-bbda-8d74f3fffe1d" 13194139535229 true] [17592186338758 1017 #edb/ref 17592186338759 13194139535229 true] [17592186338758 1089 "q-33194" 13194139535229 true] [17592186338758 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535229 true] [17592186338758 1100 "Find the intersection point of the line $l$ and the plane $Π$ with equations\n\n$$\nl:r=⟨2,1,0⟩+t⟨1,3,2⟩,\\,Π:3x-2y+4z+6=0.\n$$" 13194139535229 true] [17592186338758 1113 #uuid "095e7ba7-485c-5158-9e30-e0ada8d73941" 13194139535229 true] [17592186338758 1145 "Let's start by writing the equation of the line as\n\n$$\nr=⟨2+t,1+3t,2t⟩.\n$$\n\nLet's also write the equation of the plane in the dot product form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3x-2y+4z+6 & =0 \\\\ 3x-2y+4z & =-6 \\\\ ⟨x,y,z⟩\\cdot ⟨3,-2,4⟩ & =-6 \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨3,-2,4⟩ & =-6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, substituting $r=⟨2+t,1+3t,2t⟩$ into the equation of the plane, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r\\cdot ⟨3,-2,4⟩ & =-6 \\\\ ⟨2+t,1+3t,2t⟩\\cdot ⟨3,-2,4⟩ & =-6 \\\\ 3(2+t)-2(1+3t)+4(2t) & =-6 \\\\ 6+3t-2-6t+8t & =-6 \\\\ 5t & =-10 \\\\ t & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, to get the position vector $p$ of the intersection point $P,$ we substitute $t=-2$ into the equation of the line:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p & =⟨2+(-2),1+3(-2),2(-2)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,-5,-4⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the intersection point is $P(0,-5,-4).$" 13194139535229 true] [17592186338759 1000 #edb/ref 17592186338760 13194139535229 true] [17592186338759 1000 #edb/ref 17592186338761 13194139535229 true] [17592186338759 1000 #edb/ref 17592186338762 13194139535229 true] [17592186338759 1000 #edb/ref 17592186338763 13194139535229 true] [17592186338759 1000 #edb/ref 17592186338764 13194139535229 true] [17592186338759 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535229 true] [17592186338759 1041 "selection" 13194139535229 true] [17