ed}|j+|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 6\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =-24i+8j+6k \\\\  & =⟨-24,8,6⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation of the plane $Π$ in dot product form is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r\\cdot n & =p\\cdot n \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨-24,8,6⟩ & =⟨-12,10,6⟩\\cdot ⟨-24,8,6⟩ \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨-24,8,6⟩ & =404.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, substituting $r=⟨1,3,2⟩+w⟨-5,-2,-1⟩$ into the equation of the plane in dot product form, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r\\cdot ⟨-24,8,6⟩ & =404 \\\\ ⟨1-5w,3-2w,2-w⟩\\cdot ⟨-24,8,6⟩ & =404 \\\\ -24(1-5w)+8(3-2w)+6(2-w) & =404 \\\\ -24+120w+24-16w+12-6w & =404 \\\\ 98w & =392 \\\\ w & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, to get the position vector $q$ of the intersection point $Q,$ we substitute $w=4$ into the vector equation of the line:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}q & =⟨1-5(4),3-2(4),2-(4)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-19,-5,-2⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the intersection point is $Q(-19,-5,-2).$" 13194139535229 true] [17592186338780 1000 #edb/ref 17592186338781 13194139535229 true] [17592186338780 1000 #edb/ref 17592186338782 13194139535229 true] [17592186338780 1000 #edb/ref 17592186338783 13194139535229 true] [17592186338780 1000 #edb/ref 17592186338784 13194139535229 true] [17592186338780 1000 #edb/ref 17592186338785 13194139535229 true] [17592186338780 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535229 true] [17592186338780 1041 "selection" 13194139535229 true] [17592186338780 1104 #edb/ref 17592186338784 13194139535229 true] [17592186338780 1110 #uuid "4312fcfe-ca68-5a99-a8f2-1e923eca295b" 13194139535229 true] [17592186338781 1034 "(-5,-2,-1)" 13194139535229 true] [17592186338781 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535229 true] [17592186338781 1111 #uuid "80c089cc-0c53-590f-a42b-18de8a2f4284" 13194139535229 true] [17592186338782 1034 "(-9,-5,-2)" 13194139535229 true] [17592186338782 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535229 true] [17592186338782 1111 #uuid "cf1474a9-6277-548c-a070-2baaee6f31e9" 13194139535229 true] [17592186338783 1034 "No intersection" 1319413